    "body": "The Army is heading into AUSA 2026 with new leadership and a major question hanging over the service: How much of its modernization agenda will remain intact? Breaking Defense Editor-in-Chief Aaron Mehta and Army reporter Carley Welch preview what they expect to hear from acting Army Secretary Adam Telle and acting service chief Gen. Christopher LaNeve. Then they discuss what the Army’s new autonomy command could mean for its growing focus on drones and robots .\nMake sure to check back each day next week for wrap-up videos , photos from the show floor and comprehensive reporting from the Army’s biggest annual conference.\nBreaking Defense Video\nNew leaders, new drone command: What we expect from AUSA 2026\nWatch Now »\nUnpacking Boeing’s F/A-XX win, plus a report from wartime Ukraine\nWatch Now »\nHow Hegseth envisions a new Autonomous Warfare Command\nWatch Now »\nWhat Europe’s military air fleets will look like in 30 years\nWatch Now »\nRiyadh gets closer to F-35s, Damascus presses sovereignty and an expert take on Iran\nWatch Now »\nDrone-hunting on the border, plus turmoil at an Air Force think tank\nWatch Now »\nThe future of European airpower might be unmanned\nWatch Now »\nThe big news out of AFA, plus a guided tour of the show floor\nWatch Now »\nWhy the ‘right to repair’ matters to the Pentagon\nWatch Now »\nWhat the Pentagon is testing along the US-Mexico border\nWatch Now »\nScroll for more video",
